<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Angelina River</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Angelina River is a river of East <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> that flows south-east through the Piney Woods to join the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neches-river">Neches River</a>. It is named after Angelina, a Hasinai woman who worked as an interpreter for Spanish missionaries in the early 18th century. Its valley was part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> of the Hasinai <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caddo">Caddo</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/angelina-river.jpg" alt="Angelina River" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Billy Hathorn at English Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Angelina_River_west_of_Nacogdoches,_Texas.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
